SPECIALIST PLAN:
Plan for tour: Visit container then rock (in that order). Roles:
- navigator: Wait for scan results. When lidar reports a class centroid for the current target (first 'container', then 'rock'), navigate to a goal point at least 3 m from that centroid by computing goal = centroid + 3*(pose - centroid)/||pose - centroid|| using the current robot pose. If lidar reports no centroid for the current target, wait for planner to call get_occupancy_map; then drive to the planner-selected free cell (different quadrant from already-seen objects) and stop for another scan. Always stop before any sensing. After each commanded stop, wait for confirm_stop from lidar or camera before proceeding.
- lidar: When stationary, perform a semantic lidar scan and report any detected objects (class + centroid). After navigator stops at a tour stop, call confirm_stop(name) for the ordered class to verify the stop.
- camera: When stationary, capture RGB (and optional class histogram) and report any detections. If lidar cannot confirm a stop, camera may call confirm_stop(name) as an alternative verifier.
Notes:
- Hard distance: Navigator must never navigate to an object centroid; always use the 3 m offset toward the current robot pose.
- The planner handles occupancy map queries and will pick free cells if objects are not detected.
- Do not proceed to the rock until container is confirmed.
- After both stops are confirmed, planner will call report_mission_done(summary).
